From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000015 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: a733: put PB0-PB3 back to IO disable in the SPL

The vendor boot0 left PB0-PB3 on function 7, JTAG:
PB_CFG0 read 0xffff7777 at the U-Boot prompt. Nothing later uses JTAG
there, and on the Cubie A7S these are header pins (J11 7, 11, 29 and J6
1). The SPL sets them to their reset value, IO disable (0xf), next to the
console pins it already configures, whatever the stage before it left.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
index 2a1d719ef58..8544878bb7a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
@@ -81,6 +81,7 @@ phys_addr_t board_get_usable_ram_top(phys_size_t total_size)
 static int gpio_init(void)
 {
 	__maybe_unused uint val;
+	__maybe_unused int pin;
 #if CONFIG_CONS_INDEX == 1 && defined(CONFIG_UART0_PORT_F)
 #if defined(CONFIG_MACH_SUN4I) || \
     defined(CONFIG_MACH_SUN7I) || \
@@ -195,6 +196,12 @@ static int gpio_init(void)
 #error Unsupported console port number. Please fix pin mux settings in board.c
 #endif
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN60I_A733
+	/* boot0 leaves PB0-PB3 on JTAG; return them to IO disable */
+	for (pin = SUNXI_GPB(0); pin <= SUNXI_GPB(3); pin++)
+		sunxi_gpio_set_cfgpin(pin, SUNXI_GPIO_DISABLE);
+#endif
+
 	/*
 	 * Update PIO power bias configuration by copying the hardware
 	 * detected value.
